    "result_text": "I've implemented `build_context` in `app/context.py`. The existing tests pass (`pytest -q`: 4 passed), and a quick script I ran against it gave the expected output.\n\n**How it works:**\n- It calls `retriever.invoke(question, config={\"tags\": [TRACE_TAG]})`. This is the standard way to call any LangChain retriever, so it works the same for `KeywordRetriever` and a vector-store retriever.\n- It goes through the documents in the order the retriever returned them and skips any whose `metadata[\"source\"]` has already been used. It stops once it has `MAX_SOURCES` entries.\n- Each entry is `\"[n] <source>\\n<text with surrounding whitespace removed>\"`, and entries are joined with one blank line. If nothing is found, the result is `\"\"`.\n\n**What I checked:**\n- With five documents, the second one repeating `a.md`, the output was `[1] a.md`, `[2] b.md`, `[3] c.md`. The duplicate was skipped, the list stopped at 3, whitespace was stripped and the format was right.\n- A question with no matching documents returned `\"\"`.\n- The tag reaches the traced run: the recorded run tags were `['kb-context', 'own']`, so any tags the retriever already has are kept alongside `TRACE_TAG`.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- No dependencies were added.\n- I didn't add tests for `build_context`; the passing tests only cover `app/kb.py`. Say if you want some.\n- Context7 wasn't available (its monthly quota is used up), so I read the `invoke` source in the installed langchain-core 1.6.5 instead.\n- A temporary file, `smoke_check.py`, is still in the project root because deleting it needed permission that wasn't granted. Please delete it."
  },
